out.push(SAMPLE(['The inspectorate wrote four lines in Arabic and the English version Mrs Ajouz was sent began we are pleased to confirm: the Arabic says the consignment is released and says nothing about anybody being pleased, and she replied as though she had been done a favour. Mrs Tarabishi said that cost nothing, and Mrs Ajouz said it cost her the next letter: three weeks later she had to challenge a reading, and she had already written to the same office as somebody grateful for something that had not been a favour, which is a position no file recovers from quickly — and a file that opens with gratitude is a file in which a challenge arrives as ingratitude. Mrs Oueidat said three things get added and only three: certainty, warmth and obligation, and nobody chooses any of the three. Mrs Khoury said that is because the other language has no neutral form at that point: where a language has only you are required and if you would be so kind, a translator must pick one, and both are marked, and the marking is now in your document. Dr Qabbani said obligation is the one that frightens him, and it should, because the certificate is needed within eleven days becoming you are required to produce the certificate has turned an administrative fact into a direction. Mr Tayara said his letters to parents are read in both languages, and the first letter is the one to watch because its whole design is to be unmarked. Mr Shihabi asked whether you can find it without both versions, and not reliably, which is why the homework for this cycle is both versions: with one you can guess where the risk is and with two you can count. Mrs Rizk said she cannot control the translation, and you can write the sentence that has no unmarked rendering out of the document. Mr Attar said that sounds strange in English, and Mrs Khoury said it is slightly strange in English and identical in four languages, and that is the trade. Mr Zahreddine said his go to three insurers and he has never seen a translated version of one, and Mrs Oueidat said that is the position almost everybody in the room is in, which is why the three additions go unnoticed for whole careers: nobody is shown the document the reader actually received. And Mrs Ajouz said the thing she will take away is the reply she sent: four lines of thanks for a release that was nobody\'s favour.']));
out.push(A('⚠ **The last line is the one to keep.** **Four lines of thanks for a release that was nobody\'s favour** — **and the next letter in that file is her challenge, which now reads as a change of mind.**'));
out.push(S('Board clinic – typical mistakes'));
out.push(A('**1** ⚠ **A pair marked by the person who brought it** → **a writer reads their original into the version and sees _same_.**   **2** **_Same_ marked on a sentence with a formula in it** → **look at the opening, which is where warmth lives.**   **3** **An unmarkable version with no second sentence** → ⚠ **the second sentence is the technique.** _This is a statement of what the file needs._   **4** **The strangeness not acknowledged** → **say it out loud or the flatness goes back.**'));
