// ===================== 11.6 =====================
out.push(pb());
out.push(h2('11.6  The covering note that makes it usable'));
out.push(S('Stage 1 · Get ready'));
out.push(A('**a** Open. ⚠ **The whole of it, however short, and its length in words on the board.** **In most classes seven or eight of the ten are under forty words and contain nothing but a greeting and the word _attached_.** **The column of lengths is the argument** — **and every one of those seven accompanied a document that needed three sentences it did not get.**'));
out.push(A('**b** Belong in the note: **3** and **5**. ⚠ **3 is an absence stated as a fact about the writer\'s own system; 5 is the instruction about the order, with its reason attached.** **1, 2 and 4 are the three sentences that make up nine covering emails in ten** — **and none of them carries anything a reader could not have assumed.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 2 · Listen and read'));
out.push(A('**a** **B** — **the three absences and one instruction about how to read the document**, which is work the document itself cannot do for a reader in another system.'));
out.push(A('**b** **1** ⚠ **Thirty-one words**, and the application had four things in it with no equivalent in the donor\'s system. **The note now names three of the four and gives one instruction about the order.**   **2** **It is useful when it is about the order and presumptuous when it is about what to think** — _read 4 before 2_ **against** _please note that our figures are robust_.'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **The three-and-one shape is the deliverable and should be marked before anything else: three absences, about sixty words each, and one instruction about the order with its reason.** **Shorter than 260 words and an absence has been left out; longer than 300 and the note has become a summary, which the reader will then read instead of the document.** ⚠ **Why three, and it is not an aesthetic figure: three is what a reader will carry.** **Mrs Oueidat has sent notes with seven absences and watched a court use two.** **The three to choose are the ones where a reader will supply something confidently** — **not the three largest and not the three hardest to explain, and the students\' own marked rows from 11.1\'s homework are the right source.**'));
out.push(S('Language box · Practise'));
out.push(A('**1** **A role with no equivalent** — _there is no grants panel; two readers assess separately and do not meet._   **2** **A word read differently** — _a fixed clinic here is a building open two or three days a week._   **3** **A figure that cannot be compared** — _the two projects are comparable to each other and not to this one._   **4** ⚠ **The instruction** — _read paragraph 11 before paragraph 9_, **with the reason.**   **5** ⚠ **An instruction about what to think may not be written**, because it asks for a reading rather than an order and a reader may decline a reading.'));
out.push(S('Stage 3 · Practise (sample – Card A)'));
