out.push(NOTE('⚠ **This is the eighth and last mediation in Book 1 and the first in which nobody is at fault, so the sorting has to be done before any letter is written.** **The author did not write either sentence; the translator did what her covering line says she does and sent it; the committee read what it was given.** **The only fault in the exchange is that the covering line was filed and not circulated** — **and that is a fact about a system and belongs to nobody.** ⚠ **Never write that the translation was wrong.** **It was not, and it is the one sentence in such a letter that can be answered** — **and a letter with an answerable sentence in it produces a reply about that sentence and no resolution withdrawn.**'));
out.push(NOTE('**Separate the two resolutions and keep the useful one, because a class will ask for both to go.** ⚠ **The resolution to add the two lines should stand: it gives eighteen months of data that nobody had.** **The words _and to record that the staffing is the cause_ are the whole of what has to be withdrawn.** **A letter that asks for both loses the data as well**, and the committee then has nothing to show for two months. ⚠ **And say what was right before what was wrong** — _the committee was right about the measurement and wrong about the cause_ — **which is 7.2\'s concession at the strongest point arriving for the last time in Book 1, and a letter in that order is read to the end.**'));
